  "id": "Compound::DB01337 - Gene::1135",
  "verbalization": "Pancuronium is linked to Chrna2 through a series of molecular interactions that involve Vecuronium, a neuromuscular blocker. The evidence suggests that Pancuronium binds to Chrnb1, which in turn is bound by Vecuronium, and Vecuronium subsequently binds to Chrna2. This creates a chain of interactions that ultimately leads to the modulation of Chrna2. The lowest common ancestor of Pancuronium and Vecuronium is Acetate Ester, indicating a shared biochemical pathway. The relationship between Pancuronium and Chrna2 is thus mediated through Vecuronium, with the binding of Vecuronium to Chrna2 being a critical step in the mechanism. The evidence supports a direct interaction between Pancuronium and Chrna2, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
